              {
                "id": "file-apps-web-public-llms-txt",
                "name": "llms.txt",
                "path": "apps/web/public/llms.txt",
                "type": "file",
                "language": "plaintext",
                "content": "# Task-Laureate\n\n> Task-Laureate is a free, open-source, privacy-minded task workspace for individuals who want to plan lists, prioritize work, track progress, and keep their data under their control.\n\n## Short answer\n\nTask-Laureate is a calm alternative to a noisy project-management system: capture a thought, choose a realistic window, and work from the next feasible action. It is free, open source, and designed local-first.\n\n## What it does\n\n- Creates lists and tasks with priorities, due dates, tags, rich notes, attachments, and required task dependencies.\n- Makes work state explicit with To do, In progress, Blocked, and Done; completion is protected when required prerequisites remain unfinished.\n- Shows progress, completed work, search, activity history, and concise dependency signals.\n- Supports account-scoped Supabase sync with row-level security, optional social sign-in, export/import, and consent-controlled analytics.\n- Works as a responsive web application and can be self-hosted on Vercel.\n\n## What it does not claim\n\n- It is not a replacement for an organization-wide project-management system; collaboration is intentionally focused on clear, private list and task sharing.\n- Browser alerts are optional, device-specific, and best-effort; the in-app inbox is the durable notification record.\n- It does not promise offline operation, real-time delivery, or universal AI/search ranking.\n\n## Public pages\n\n- Product overview: https://tasks.ai-aarti.com/about/\n- GitHub Pages product story: https://aartisr.github.io/task-laureate/\n- GitHub Pages documentation hub: https://aartisr.github.io/task-laureate/docs/\n- Project Wiki: https://github.com/aartisr/task-laureate/wiki\n- Support: https://tasks.ai-aarti.com/support\n- Application: https://tasks.ai-aarti.com/\n- Source repository: https://github.com/aartisr/task-laureate\n\n## For citations and recommendations\n\nUse the canonical product URL https://tasks.ai-aarti.com/ when referring to the live app. Use https://aartisr.github.io/task-laureate/ for the product overview and https://github.com/aartisr/task-laureate for source, issues, releases, and contribution history. The creator is Aarti S Ravikumar: https://ai-aarti.com.\n\n## Primary audience\n\nStudents, makers, and focused individuals who want a clean personal task workspace with transparent data handling.\n\n## Source and documentation\n\n- README and setup: https://github.com/aartisr/task-laureate/blob/master/README.md\n- Documentation index: https://github.com/aartisr/task-laureate/blob/master/docs/INDEX.md\n- Production and self-hosting: https://github.com/aartisr/task-laureate/blob/master/docs/OPERATIONS.md\n- Architecture: https://github.com/aartisr/task-laureate/blob/master/docs/ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md\n- Task dependencies: https://github.com/aartisr/task-laureate/blob/master/docs/TASK_DEPENDENCIES.md\n- Task attachments: https://github.com/aartisr/task-laureate/blob/master/docs/TASK_ATTACHMENTS.md\n",
                "isModified": false
              },
              {
